{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities","id":832348,"title":"Fictional Examples of Peak Solar Abilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-17T23:26:39-08:00","id":832348,"title":"Fictional Examples of Peak Solar Abilities","content":"So going over the Exalted Solar Charms and am seeing a lot of suggestive influence of source material for what brought some ideas to fruition. So thought I'd start posting some here to share what I've discovered as possible inspirations for players wanting to know what is on offer.<br /> <br /> Though in addition, thought I'd also add some influences that aren't as obvious, but would fit the idea of a Solar hero demonstrating Solar level power in that field. At the least some conflict can be brought up to question if something is appropriate for a Solar or if it would fit a different Exalt-type better (or even not-at-all).<br /> <br /> This list started with just my own ideas, but its since become a bit of a compilation. Lets see where it goes: <hr /><br /> Archery<ul><li>Green Arrow</li> <li>Hawkeye</li> <li>Legolas</li> </ul>Athletics<ul><li>Conan</li> <li>Hercules</li> <li>The Flash</li> </ul>Awareness<ul><li>Legolas</li> <li>Wolverine (his nose)</li> </ul>Brawl<ul><li>Conan</li> <li>Hercules</li> <li>Goku/ Kakarot</li> <li>Vegeta</li> </ul>Craft<ul><li>Edward Elric (Full Metal Alchemist)</li> <li>Doctor Doom</li> </ul>Integrity<ul><li>Batman</li> <li>Jesus</li> </ul>Investigation<ul><li>Batman</li> <li>Sherlock Holmes</li> </ul>Larceny<ul><li>Artful Dodger</li> <li>Professor Moriarty</li> <li>Hoodini</li> </ul>Medicine<ul><li>Doctor Greg House</li> <li>Jesus</li> </ul>Occult<ul><li>Jesus</li> <li>Merlin</li> <li>Gandalf</li> </ul>Resistance<ul><li>Deadpool</li> <li>Wolverine</li> </ul>Socialize<ul><li>The Doctor (TImelord)</li> <li>Jaquen H'ghar (Game of Thrones)</li> <li>Little Finger (Game of Thrones)</li> </ul>Stealth<ul><li>Batman</li> </ul>War<ul><li>Alexander the Great</li> <li>Aragorn</li> <li>Leonidas (of Sparta)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":5915,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","user":"zenvious","date":". 02-18-2016, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T00:11:43-08:00","id":832370,"title":"","content":"There's a huge difference between &quot;Solar levels of power&quot; and &quot;has all the Solar Charms of this Ability up to the capstone.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say Conan's a good fit for Solar Resistance and Athletics both, and has a good number of Brawl Charms on his sheet. Heracles likewise is a great example of Solar Brawl, particularly the wrestling Charms. Jesus is Integrity, Medicine, Occult, and has sorcery to boot. Batman's a great example of Stealth In addition to the examples you gave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T01:16:23-08:00","id":832389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities?p=832370#post832370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a huge difference between &quot;Solar levels of power&quot; and &quot;has all the Solar Charms of this Ability up to the capstone.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say Conan's a good fit for Solar Resistance and Athletics both, and has a good number of Brawl Charms on his sheet. Heracles likewise is a great example of Solar Brawl, particularly the wrestling Charms. Jesus is Integrity, Medicine, Occult, and has sorcery to boot. Batman's a great example of Stealth In addition to the examples you gave.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats a fair call.<br /> <br /> Good names though! Will add them to the list - make it into a more &quot;compilation&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Jesus does bring up a very good point. What other characters have had a &quot;Rebirthing&quot; element to their history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T06:47:31-08:00","id":832483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities?p=832389#post832389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jesus does bring up a very good point. What other characters have had a &quot;Rebirthing&quot; element to their history?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gandalf<br /> <br /> Aslan - Can a Lion exalt as a Solar? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T00:33:48-08:00","id":833090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rama said slowly, &quot;The ocean is arrogant, Lakshmana. It seems that in this age of the world, the pacific way of sama is ineffectual. Even the Lords of the elements have regard only for violence, and honor is to be had only from fear. Varuna does not understand my gentleness, or he should have stood before us by now. But since he seems to believe I am a weakling, whose prayers are not worth hearing, I will change my method.<br /> &quot;Bring me my bow, Lakshmana. Let us see what Varuna does when I make vapor of his waters with my astras, and all his fish lie heaving on an arid bed of sand. The vanaras will walk on dry land to Lank, where my Sita waits in anguish for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Quietly, Lakshaman fetched the bow and quiver. Rama stood forth on that shore like the fire at the end of the yugas. He folded his hands briefly to the ocean. Assuming the archer's stance, alidha, he fitted arrow after arrow to his bow, and they flashed whistling at the waves.<br /> <br /> The sky grew dark as twilight. Thunder echoed in the darkness, and supernaturally vivid lightning divided the sky in jagged gashes. Rama's shafts of light and flames flew hissing into the waves risen like giant shields to meet them. His arrows pierced the waves as common barbs do flesh. In amazement, in fear, Lakshmana and the vanaras heard the ocean screaming above the roar of its tide, in a cavernous voice. They heard Rama roar like an angry god. They heard the report of his bowstring, again and again.<br /> <br /> The earth shook. They sky was agitated and waves rose like mountains in the stricken sea, tall as Mandara or Kailasa. The monkeys lost their nerve at the awesome violence; most of them fled screaming up Mahendra. Rama stood like a flame himself on the shore. The ocean howled back at him in pain and fury. But the arrows raged from his hands, a river of fire in spate. Whales, sea serpents, and schools of brilliant fish leaped above the seething water in terror. But they could not escape; all the ocean burned. Hilly flames danced beneath its surface, in the belly of the Lord of waves.<br /> <br /> A shocked Lakshmana fell at his brother's feet and clutched his hand. He cried, &quot;Abandon this wrath, Rama! Return to the peaceful paths of our fathers. You can win this war without laying waste the sea.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the dark sea there rose a great lament, and a hundred heavenly voices cried to the prince of light, &quot;Rama, do not dry up the ancient sea.&quot;<br /> <br /> But Rama heard neither his brother nor the supernal ones. He snatched his hand from Lakshmana, and the river of flames flowed again from his bow. In a terrible voice that was hardly his, gentle Rama roared, &quot;Varuna! I will make a desert of you and the vanaras shall cross into Lanka over your dry corpse.&quot;<br /> <br /> He paused his prodigious archery, then cried again, &quot;I will consume you and the Patalas below you. All your denizens, fish, and whale, shark and timmingala, will lie rotting under the sun.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then, standing like a burning rock upon the tempestuous beach, Rama invoked the brahmastra. It seemed earth and sky would crack open when he chanted the mantra to summon that weapon into his hands. The twilight of the world turned to a night of dread. The sun and moon strayed dizziliy from their orbits. At midmorning, stars twinkled down clearly on the earth. A thousand meteors scorched down into the hissing water. All the slow and stable elements seemed ready to come undone, at the very quick of themselves, where the grace of creation held them bound in time. Chaos verged on the world.<br /> <br /> Gale winds from the sea uprooted knotted old trees and blew them about like wisps of straw. Streaks of lightning fell out of the heavens, their rutilant whiplashes seeming to begin in the stars. Woven into the roar of the storm rang the piteous cries of the beasts of the earth, among them Sugriva's vanaras. Lions and tigers whimpered like frightened cats, and great bears wept for fear in their caves. The weaker, gentler animals were in an absolute frenzy. They dashed about blindly, shrieking, but found no refuge from Rama's ubiquitous rage.<br /> <br /> As Lakshmana watched in disbelief, the ocean receded from the shore; like a whipped cur the sea fled from Rama's fury. A yojana of dry seabed lay exposed, its pale expanse strewn with the piteous carcasses of its creatures. Dolphin and shark, great whale, whale-eating giant squid, and floundering fish of every hue and size all lay gasping their last on the desert of Rama's anger. </div> </div> </div>Hawkeye. Pfft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T04:25:41-08:00","id":833151,"title":"","content":"Dodge didn't get mentioned, but Jubei from <b>Ninja Scroll</b> is actually someone who comes to mind a bit for that one. Speed of Sound Sonic from <b>One Punch Man</b> is kinda technically/sorta another. Ninjas in general really work rather well, to be honest.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T04:44:48-08:00","id":833155,"title":"","content":"Daredevil? For all non-sight based Awareness things at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:01:48-08:00","id":833161,"title":"","content":"Solar Level Craft: Tony &quot;I built an arc reactor and a mech suit in a cave from scrap&quot; Stark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:08:58-08:00","id":833168,"title":"","content":"Apparently, a Solar exaltation can only attach itself to the Y-chromosome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:26:35-08:00","id":833178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities?p=833168#post833168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, a Solar exaltation can only attach itself to the Y-chromosome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh ?<br /> <br /> :look at the list in the OP&quot; Oooooh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:47:24-08:00","id":833190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities?p=833168#post833168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, a Solar exaltation can only attach itself to the Y-chromosome.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, its a problem. I'm struggling to come up with any superlatively skilled female characters that don't play second fiddle to a more skilled guy, don't rely heavily on magic or exotic tools, aren't characters I made myself (e.g. FemShep), and have a specialty that isn't &quot;looking pretty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:48:27-08:00","id":833191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities?p=833168#post833168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, a Solar exaltation can only attach itself to the Y-chromosome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agent Carter - Investigation<br /> Princess Leia - Integrity (with stand torture and the only Skywalker to not be tempted by the dark side) <br /> Jessica Jones - Athletics <br /> Black Widow - Socialize (for her ability to talk information about of people)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:04:46-08:00","id":833197,"title":"","content":"Looking pretty isn't a sin, mind, especially when you can leverage it the way some characters can.<br /> <br /> And heading in the opposite direction, I'd nominate Brienne of Tarth, both for the Integrity required to put up with constant showers of misogynistic bullshit, and probably for Melee as well, given her fight with one of the most storied knights alive.<br /> <br /> Arya's a good candidate for Solar Exaltation too (and PCdom in general), picking up Melee and Dodge and Athletics and Awareness and Stealth and Survival and Socialize and Larceny. None to 5 just yet, but she's putting them to pretty awesome use. <i>Valar morghulis.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-19-2016, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:08:21-08:00","id":833199,"title":"","content":"Jessica Jones is who I thought of for Athletics as well, actually. <br /> <br /> Queen Himeko in various incarnations has been great for Occult, Presence or Archery.<br /> <br /> Catwoman is pretty great at Larceny, as well as Athletics, Dodge, Presence and Socialize at various points.<br /> <br /> Balsa from <b>Guardian of the Sacred Spirit</b> is actually a pretty great Melee expert focusing on more the control/defensive stuff of the Ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar: the Last Airbender</b> has actually quite a few pretty awesome examples with women of great skill who aren't obviously magical benders about. Suki has good examples of Athletics, Dodge and Martial Arts. Ty Lee Athletics, Dodge, Martial Arts and Medicine (pressure point stuff). Mai has Thrown up the wazzoo. Jun has Melee and Survival. And in the <b>Legend of Korra</b> stuff, Asami is pretty good example of Craft-as-engineer I think with iterations and smaller project stuff.<br /> <br /> Cibo from <b>Blame!</b> is probably pretty sci-fi bent on things, but has a lot of the general Twilight Abilities to her. She'd be a neat example of an Autochthonian Exalting as a Solar, if anything.<br /> <br /> Canaan of the anime <b>Canaan</b> is pretty great example of Athletics, Awareness and Dodge, actually. She's good with shooting and such, but a lot of that comes as a result of the other bits. <br /> <br /> Togame of <b>Katanagatari</b> is actually a pretty interesting example of bits of Lore, Socialize and War all rolled together. Mostly Socialize though, since there's a lot with dialog in that show and I think her ultimate plans and plots often being based around manipulating people and their wants all fits Socialize rather well.<br /> <br /> Morgiana of <b>Magi</b> is pretty good at kicking the shit out of things and beating them up with heavy chains. I'd say she's a pretty solid Brawl example.<br /> <br /> And stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:28:51-08:00","id":833207,"title":"","content":"Maybe the problem is that most of the media i consume are videogames... <br /> <br /> Faith, from Mirror's Edge - Athletics.<br /> Vivienne, from Dragon Age: Inquisition - Socialize.<br /> Josephine, from Dragon Age: Inquisition - Bureaucracy.<br /> Katya, from Clandestine - Larceny.<br /> Nisha the Lawbringer from Borderlands: The Pre-Sequel - Firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-19-2016, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:31:46-08:00","id":833208,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add Rey from the Force Awakens to the list, under Linguistcs, Sail and Integrity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities?p=833199#post833199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morgiana of <b>Magi</b> is pretty good at kicking the shit out of things and beating them up with heavy chains. I'd say she's a pretty solid Brawl example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morgiana's stand-alone-episode (I think it's ep6 of the series) is actually one of my prime go-to-examples of a Solar character/exaltation, and setting example for new players. Though I usually go with her as a Athletics supernal Zenith (complete with visitation from UC-Sun during her moment of exaltation. It's great)<br /> <br /> Also: Balsa, hell yeah! First episode of Guardian of the Spirit is my second go-to. It's such a perfect example of an ecample PC; you get a aperfect introduction and just enough backstory to start going. It's perfect.<br /> <br /> Edit: Trying to think of some industrious villain to put as a Bureaucracy example. Thinking Ragyo from Kill la Kill, or Nicole Horne from the first Max Payne game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","user":"Kim","date":". 02-19-2016, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:46:24-08:00","id":833216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/832348-fictional-examples-of-peak-solar-abilities?p=833207#post833207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the problem is that most of the media i consume are videogames...<br /> <br /> Faith, from Mirror's Edge - Athletics.<br /> Vivienne, from Dragon Age: Inquisition - Socialize.<br /> Josephine, from Dragon Age: Inquisition - Bureaucracy.<br /> Katya, from Clandestine - Larceny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly read novels/short stories, so there is a bit more choice in female characters<br /> <br /> Lessa (Dragonriders of Pern) - Presence<br /> Menolly (Dragonriders of Pern) - Performance<br /> Tiffany Aching (Discworld) - Occult<br /> Ayla (Children of the Earth) - Linguistics, maybe Craft<br /> Molly Carpenter (Dresden Files) - Occult<br /> Karrin Murphy (Dresden Files) - Integrity<br /> Catherine Harcourt (Tremaire) - Ride<br /> Jane Roland (Tremaire) - Ride, maybe War<br /> <br /> I want to add Anyanwu from Wild Seed for Medicine, but she is definitely Lunar (She manufactures the Medicines in her body). Doro would be her Abyssal Mate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-19-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T17:40:02-08:00","id":833611,"title":"","content":"I'm wracking my brain trying to think what Red Sonja would have 5 in. but, not coming up with much as far as abilities (just 5 appearence and stamina)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}